 Overview

Smart Scheduler is a Python-based study planning backend built with FastAPI and MySQL, designed to provide a foundation for organizing study sessions, generating weekly study plans, managing user accounts, and tracking study progress through RESTful API endpoints. The application follows a modular structure that separates API routing, database connectivity, and authentication utilities, making its core components easier to maintain and extend. User management incorporates password hashing and JSON Web Token (JWT) authentication, while study-session endpoints support creating and retrieving session records associated with individual users. A progress-tracking module calculates session completion statistics, and the planner provides an initial subject-distribution mechanism across six days of the week. Uvicorn serves the application as an ASGI web service, with deployment configuration provided through a Procfile. The project establishes a foundation for a more comprehensive study planning system, with further development focused on secure user-specific data access, robust scheduling algorithms, input validation, and personalized study planning based on priorities, available time, and learning goals.
